<!-- Real Ford varb vertical simulation: all 182 samples; only mapped KnC channels retained.
     Source: ford-b479-data/simulations/varb/varb-lommel-2up-knc-vertical-b1e0f1_spmm.res
     Values and units are unchanged; component IDs are densely renumbered.
     til_wheel_contact_patch/tir_wheel_contact_patch x_front/y_front/x_rear/y_rear
     are NOT from that source (it has no contact-patch channel at this sample
     count) -- they are wheel_center_rise_*_wrt_body x/y scaled by a constant
     per corner (front x *1.4, front y *-1.3, rear x/y *1.0), derived from the
     real wheel-center-to-contact-patch ratio seen in the full VARB/VARC
     vertical+static .res files, so brake_support_angle has something to
     compute here. Not a measured signal. -->
